{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 9.047,
   "text": "When I moved into apartment 4C, there was a strip of black tape over the peephole."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.647,
   "end": 16.857,
   "text": "The super told me it stays there. Never peel it off. And never look out after two in the morning... no matter who knocks."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 17.557,
   "end": 20.8,
   "text": "I thought he was joking. He wasn't smiling."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.7,
   "end": 25.711,
   "text": "The first knock came on a Tuesday. Two-oh-one A.M."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 26.311,
   "end": 29.404,
   "text": "Two soft taps... right at eye level."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.004,
   "end": 36.441,
   "text": "Then a whisper through the crack of the door. It's okay... you can look."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 37.641,
   "end": 42.676,
   "text": "It came back every night. Same time. Same taps. Same patient voice."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 43.476,
   "end": 49.577,
   "text": "On the ninth night, I couldn't take it anymore. I peeled back the tape... and pressed my eye to the glass."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 50.477,
   "end": 53.656,
   "text": "Nothing. Just a dark, blurry circle."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.656,
   "end": 56.683,
   "text": "Then the circle blinked."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 59.083,
   "end": 65.461,
   "text": "This morning I told the super. He unscrewed the peephole, turned it over in his hand... and went very quiet."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 66.461,
   "end": 69.213,
   "text": "It had been installed backwards."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 70.613,
   "end": 74.283,
   "text": "That tape was never there to stop me from looking out."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 75.183,
   "end": 78.361,
   "text": "It was there to stop something from looking in."
  }
 ],
